Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 01/20/2024]
1. Excitation energies from ENSDF, except that we disregarded three listed levels: (i) Ex = 1553 keV; we assume that this is the same as Ex = 1538 keV (only a 
   single level is reported in Visser et al. 2007); (ii) Ex = 1645 keV; this is presumably the same as Ex = 1617 keV (only a single level is reported in Visser et 
   al. 2007); (iii) Ex = 2605 keV; this (1+) level was reported by Zegers et al. 2008; however, it was neither observed by Visser et al. 2007, nor does the 
   shell-model predict a 1+ level in this excitation energy range; see discussion in Zegers et al. 2008.
2. We calculate the resonant rate contributions from partial widths and mirror state information; for Er = 482 keV, the indirectly obtained strength agrees with
   the directly measured one by Erikson et al. 2010.
3. Mirror state assignments are based on Herndl et al. 1998 and Lotay et al. 2008.
4. C2S values from Endt 1977 and Tomandl et al. 2004.
5. For Er = 660 and 942 keV, the lifetimes of the 24Na mirror levels are not known; for these two resonances the gamma-ray partial widths were adopted from
   shell-model results (Herndl et al. 1998).
6. Direct capture is estimated using experimental C2S values of mirror states in 24Na.
